        "summary": "Nebius Group N.V. (NBIS) stock fell by about 8% to $99.12, dropping below $100 after reaching $108 earlier in the session. This decline is attributed to investor concerns over the funding and execution risks associated with Nebius's ambitious 2026 build-out plan, which includes $16 billion to $20 billion in capital expenditure and adding nine new data-center sites. Despite recent bullish coverage and increased options activity, the market is scrutinizing the company's ability to finance and implement its growth strategy without significant shareholder dilution or operational stumbles.",
