        "summary": "Micron Technology (MU) has transformed into a critical component of the AI infrastructure, moving beyond its cyclical past due to high demand for High Bandwidth Memory (HBM) and enterprise storage. The company is experiencing a \"structural supercycle,\" driven by its technological leadership in HBM3E and HBM4, and bolstered by significant U.S. government subsidies. CEO Sanjay Mehrotra's leadership has shifted the company's focus to high-margin AI applications, resulting in strong financial performance and a bullish investor outlook despite geopolitical and market cyclicality risks.",
