        "summary": "This Form 424B2 filing by Barclays Bank PLC details the offering of $1,026,000 Contingent Coupon Barrier Notes due February 16, 2029, linked to the performance of the Nasdaq-100, Russell 2000, and S&P 500 Indices. The notes offer contingent coupon payments based on the performance of the least performing index but do not guarantee principal repayment or fixed interest, exposing investors to potential significant losses including 100% of the principal at maturity. The document outlines the terms, risks, tax considerations, and includes a consent to U.K. Bail-in Power, highlighting that payments are subject to Barclays Bank PLC's creditworthiness and regulatory actions.",
