        "summary": "Short interest in the State Street Technology Select Sector SPDR ETF (XLK) has nearly tripled in two months, driven by its high concentration in AI-heavy mega-cap stocks like Nvidia, Apple, and Microsoft. This rise suggests that institutional investors are hedging against concentration risk, rather than broadly betting against the tech sector, as short interest in the broader Invesco QQQ Trust (QQQ) has simultaneously fallen. The low days-to-cover ratios for XLK shorts further indicate calculated risk management rather than panic shorting.",
