        "summary": "Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) is trying to catch up in the AI accelerator market, but analysts like Gil Luria of DA Davidson remain cautious. Despite strong paper specifications for AMD's Instinct GPUs, market success depends heavily on interconnect and systems-integration, areas where Nvidia holds a significant advantage. This leads to lower real-world performance for AMD's hardware and suggests that customers, including major players like OpenAI, prefer competing technologies over AMD's offerings for frontier AI workloads.",
