        "url": "https://fortune.com/2026/02/15/ai-demand-memory-chip-shortage-crisis-dram-hbm-micron-skhynix-samsung/",
        "time_published": "20260216T004416",
        "authors": [
            "Debby Wu",
            "Takashi Mochizuki",
            "Yoolim Lee",
            "Bloomberg"
        ],
        "summary": "The booming demand for AI-driven memory chips, especially high-bandwidth memory (HBM), is causing a severe global shortage of Dynamic Random Access Memory (DRAM). This crisis is impacting various industries, leading to soaring prices, production constraints for electronics manufacturers like Apple and Sony, and prompting warnings from tech leaders about a prolonged \"super-cycle\" of AI demand disrupting traditional supply and demand dynamics. Companies are now prioritizing HBM production for AI accelerators, leaving less capacity for standard DRAM used in everyday electronics.",
