        "summary": "Nvidia has announced a multiyear deal to supply Meta Platforms with millions of its current and future AI chips, including central processing units designed to compete with Intel and AMD. The agreement encompasses Nvidia's Blackwell and forthcoming Rubin AI chips, as well as its Grace and Vera central processors. This move highlights Nvidia's strategy to expand its chip offerings beyond AI into areas like database management and to solidify its business relationship with Meta, despite Meta's own AI chip development efforts.",
