        "url": "https://markets.financialcontent.com/stocks/article/marketminute-2026-2-16-the-saaspocalypse-of-2026-why-applovin-and-ciscos-record-earnings-are-falling-on-deaf-ears",
        "time_published": "20260216T115300",
        "authors": [
            "MarketMinute"
        ],
        "summary": "Despite reporting record earnings, AppLovin and Cisco experienced significant stock sell-offs in February 2026, signaling a \"SaaSpocalypse\" driven by the market's re-evaluation of software companies in the face of autonomous AI. Investors are shifting focus from current profitability to long-term \"terminal value,\" questioning the sustainability of traditional software-as-a-service (SaaS) models as AI agents threaten to disintermediate human workflows and seat-based licensing. The market is now segmenting between AI enablers and those disrupted, with a new emphasis on \"outcome-based\" pricing and \"gross margin per AI-hour\" as critical metrics for survival in the emerging \"Agent Economy.\"",
