        "summary": "Interdigital, a major patent holder in 5G, is cautioning against adopting a new waveform called orthogonal time frequency space (OTFS) for 6G's integrated sensing and communication (ISAC) features. The company argues that switching from the current orthogonal frequency division multiplexing (OFDM) waveform would be highly disruptive to existing 4G and 5G network infrastructure. While OTFS proponents claim it offers superior ISAC capabilities and backward compatibility, Interdigital believes OFDM can achieve similar benefits and emphasizes the significant investments already made in OFDM-based technologies by operators and device manufacturers.",
