        "summary": "AGNC Investment (NASDAQ: AGNC) offers a substantial 12.5% dividend yield, much higher than the S&P 500 or average REITs. However, AGNC operates more like a bond mutual fund than a traditional REIT by investing in mortgage-backed securities, leading to volatile dividends and a declining stock price over time. While not ideal for income-focused investors, AGNC can deliver strong total returns if dividends are reinvested, potentially offering diversification benefits.",
