        "authors": [
            "Sam Boughedda"
        ],
        "summary": "Morgan Stanley has increased its 2026 U.S. GDP growth forecast from 2.4% to 2.6%, citing stronger capital expenditure (capex) assumptions driven by rising hyperscaler spending. The bank's equity analysts revised their 2026 and 2027 hyperscaler capex estimates significantly upwards, influencing nonresidential business fixed investment projections. This revised outlook, supported by resilient consumer spending and firm business investment, also projects higher productivity growth, though it warns of potential risks if AI-driven investment returns do not materialize.",
